\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.4}{\ignorespaces Left: initial frame, right: final frame. The water molecules are displayed as transparent, blue balls. Lipid bilayer has clearly formed, with the lipid heads facing the water and the lipid tails buried! A comment: for any serious research simulation, you would need much more water molecules. Because here there are too few and the upper leaflet of the lipid is still influenced by the lower one. The water layer separating the two is not tick enough. But still, this looks incredible. }}{94}{figure.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
