\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.7}{\ignorespaces Thickness: $4.6395$ nm. Describe what you see: the density of carbon has a slight decrease in correspondence of the end of the first lipid leaflet and start of the second. There is a small "gap" of empty space there. The water still penetrate for a while after the phosphate group peaks. }}{99}{figure.caption.55}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{6. Order parameter}{99}{figure.caption.55}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.8}{\ignorespaces Results: order parameter evolution during the equilibration run, for various bonds. The head group bonds have two different behaviours, with $NC3-P04$ being mostly parallel to the surface while the next one, $P04-GL1$ is mostly perpendicular to the surface. Instead, the tails - as expected - extend straight(ish) into the perpendicular direction.}}{100}{figure.caption.57}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.9}{\ignorespaces A visual inspection of some DSPC molecules after equilibration (\texttt  {dspc-pr.gro}) confirms that the values of $P_2$ obtained through the automated script should be correct. }}{100}{figure.caption.58}\protected@file@percent }
